  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday through Tuesday) \nIssued at 140 AM MDT Wed Aug 26 2026\n\nThis weekend the upper high will drift eastward, centering over\nthe Mississippi River valley by Sunday, while an upper level\ntrough persists on the west coast, drawing a more traditional \nplume of monsoon moisture north and northeastward over the \nforecast area. Storm coverage will increase over central and\nwestern areas Saturday, then spread to include eastern areas as\nwell Sunday and Monday. As is typical during monsoon surges, the\nmountains and continental divide will be favored for the most \nstorms each day. On Tuesday, storm coverage is forecast to\ndecrease again as the upper high tries to recenter over the\nsouthern NM/Mexico border. This would not only cutoff the monsoon\nflow, but move some drier air over the state from the west.\n\nWith the increased monsoon moisture, the forecast area will take a\nbreak from near-record warmth for a while, but highs will still \nclimb as much as 12 degrees above average over eastern areas.",
